Notebook[{Cell["Transverse spin transfer at Born level in parton-parton \
scattering: the resolved-photon channels", "Title"], 
  Cell["The lowest-order transverse-spin-transfer squares of the massless 2 \
-> 2 QCD channels a(pa) b(pb) -> c(p) d(pd) with the first incoming parton \
transversely polarized and the transverse spin of the tagged parton c \
measured, needed as the resolved-photon Born terms of the Collins asymmetry \
(Eq. (resolved-transverse-born) of the paper).  As in Processes/PartonicBorn: \
s = (pa+pb)^2, t = (pa-p)^2, u = (pb-p)^2, s + t + u = 0; the result is \
divided by gs^4; the spins and colours of b are averaged, those of d summed; \
the same FeynArts generation and polarization sums.  The transverse \
projections are those of 2-Algebra-FeynCalc.wl with pa in place of the \
polarized quark k and pb in place of the lepton l: T = sigma(a up -> c up) - \
sigma(a up -> c down), density pa-slash gamma5 a-slash/2 for a (the same \
expression for an incoming antiquark, v(s) vbar(s) = p-slash (1 + gamma5 \
s-slash)/2) and the projection p-slash gamma5 b-slash for c (quark or \
antiquark), with the normal axis (T_NN) and the in-plane axes (T_XX), and the \
Collins projection (T_NN + T_XX)/2.  A tagged gluon carries no transversity; \
transfer to a quark of another flavour must vanish (control channels: q qp -> \
qp, q qb -> qp, q qb -> qpb and their charge conjugates, so that the table \
holds every channel together with its charge conjugate).\n\nExpected (the \
paper, with K = (Nc^2-1)/Nc^2, in four dimensions): q q' -> q and q qb' -> q: \
-K s u/t^2;  q q -> q: -K s u/t^2 + K s/(Nc t);  q qb -> q: -K s u/t^2 + K \
u/(Nc t);  q qb -> qb: -K/Nc;  q g -> q: -2 s u/t^2 + K; the charge-conjugate \
channels have the same values.", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["LoadFeynCalc[]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Channels and diagrams", "Section"], Cell["field = <|\"q\" -> F[3, \
{1}], \"qb\" -> -F[3, {1}], \"qp\" -> F[3, {2}], \"qpb\" -> -F[3, {2}], \"g\" \
-> V[5]|>;\nexcluded = {S[_], U[_], V[1 | 2 | 3], F[1 | 2 | 4], F[3, \
{3}]};\nrepresentatives = {{\"q\", \"qp\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qpb\", \"q\"}, \
{\"q\", \"q\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"q\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"qb\"}, \
{\"q\", \"g\", \"q\"}};\ncontrols = {{\"q\", \"qp\", \"qp\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \
\"qp\"}, {\"q\", \"qb\", \"qpb\"}};\nconjugate[x_] := x /. {\"q\" -> \"qb\", \
\"qb\" -> \"q\", \"qp\" -> \"qpb\", \"qpb\" -> \"qp\"};\nchannels = \
Join[representatives, controls, conjugate /@ representatives, conjugate /@ \
controls];\nname[{a_, b_, c_}] := a <> \" \" <> b <> \" -> \" <> \
c;\nflavourNumber[x_] := Switch[x, \"q\", {1, 0}, \"qb\", {-1, 0}, \"qp\", \
{0, 1}, \"qpb\", {0, -1}, \"g\", {0, 0}];\npartner[{a_, b_, c_}] := \
Module[{ok = Select[Keys[field], Total[flavourNumber /@ {a, b}] === \
Total[flavourNumber /@ {c, #}] &]},\n  Require[Length[ok] == 1, \"The \
unobserved parton of \" <> name[{a, b, c}] <> \" is not unique\", ok]; \
First[ok]];\ndiagrams = Association @ Table[name[ch] -> \
InsertFields[CreateTopologies[0, 2 -> 2],\n  {field[ch[[1]]], field[ch[[2]]]} \
-> {field[ch[[3]]], field[partner[ch]]},\n  InsertionLevel -> {Classes}, \
Model -> \"SMQCD\", ExcludeParticles -> excluded], {ch, \
channels}];\nMap[Length, diagrams]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Squared matrix elements with the transverse projections", "Section"], 
  Cell["As in Processes/PartonicBorn: the spinors of the polarized legs are \
renamed so that the slashes FermionSpinSum produces can be replaced by the \
densities; external gluons get the physical polarization sum with a reference \
vector; colour sums by SUNSimplify.", "Text"], Cell["FCClearScalarProducts[];\
\nSetMandelstam[s, t, u, pa, pb, -p, -pd, 0, 0, 0, 0];\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - \
4] = 0) &, {pa, pb, p, pd, nn}];\nSPD[nn] = -1; SP[nn] = -1; Scan[(SPD[nn, #] \
= 0; SP[nn, #] = 0) &, {pa, pb, p, \
pd}];\nFCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\n$LeviCivitaSign = -1;\n(* the spin \
axes as vectors of their own with explicit scalar products, as in \
2-Algebra-FeynCalc.wl: aX = (t/s) pb + (u/s) pa + p, bX = t/(t+u) pb - \
u/(t+u) pa - s(u-t)/(t+u)^2 p *)\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {aX, \
bX}];\naxisCoefficients = <|aX -> {t/s, u/s, 1}, bX -> {t/(t + u), -u/(t + \
u), -s (u - t)/(t + u)^2}|>;\nDo[With[{c = axisCoefficients[axis], base = \
{pb, pa, p}},\n  Do[SP[axis, x] = SPD[axis, x] = Factor[Sum[c[[i]] \
SP[base[[i]], x], {i, 3}]], {x, {pa, pb, p, pd}}];\n  SP[axis, nn] = \
SPD[axis, nn] = 0], {axis, {aX, bX}}];\nDo[With[{c1 = \
axisCoefficients[pair[[1]]], c2 = axisCoefficients[pair[[2]]], base = {pb, \
pa, p}},\n  SP[pair[[1]], pair[[2]]] = SPD[pair[[1]], pair[[2]]] = \
Factor[Sum[c1[[i]] c2[[j]] SP[base[[i]], base[[j]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]]], \
{pair, {{aX, aX}, {bX, bX}, {aX, bX}}}];\naxes = <|\"aX\" -> aX, \"bX\" -> \
bX, \"Lengths\" -> -t u/(t + u)|>;\nRequire[Simplify[{SP[aX, pb], SP[aX, pa], \
SP[bX, p], SP[bX, pa] + SP[bX, pb], SP[aX] + t u/s, SP[bX] + s t u/(t + u)^2} \
/. u -> -s - t] === {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},\n  \"The in-plane axes are not what \
the text says\"];\namplitude[ch_] := \
Total[FCFAConvert[CreateFeynAmp[diagrams[name[ch]], Truncated -> False, \
PreFactor -> 1],\n  IncomingMomenta -> {pa, pb}, OutgoingMomenta -> {p, pd}, \
UndoChiralSplittings -> True, ChangeDimension -> D,\n  List -> True, SMP -> \
False, Contract -> False, DropSumOver -> True,\n  FinalSubstitutions -> \
{FCGV[\"MU\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MC\"] -> 0}] /. SMP[\"g_s\"] -> gs /. GaugeXi[_] \
-> 1];\nreference = <|pa -> pb, pb -> pa, p -> pa, pd -> \
pa|>;\npolarizationSum[l_, mu_, nu_] := With[{r = reference[l]}, -MTD[mu, nu] \
+ (FVD[l, mu] FVD[r, nu] + FVD[r, mu] FVD[l, nu])/SPD[l, r]];\naverage[ch_] \
:= 1/2 Switch[ch[[2]], \"g\", 1/(D - 2)/(Nc^2 - 1), _, 1/(2 Nc)] \
Switch[ch[[1]], \"g\", 1/(Nc^2 - 1), _, 1/Nc];   (* 1/2: the fixed spin of a \
*)\ncolourFactors[expr_] := Factor[expr /. SUNN -> Nc];\ntag[l_] := \
Symbol[ToString[l] <> \"Spin\"];\nspinVectors = <|\"NN\" -> {nn, nn}, \"XX\" \
-> {axes[\"aX\"], axes[\"bX\"]}|>;\nsquare[ch_, spinCase_] := Module[{amp = \
amplitude[ch], conj, expr, gluons, indices, sa, sc},\n  {sa, sc} = \
spinVectors[spinCase];\n  gluons = Union[Cases[amp, Polarization[l_, __] :> \
l, Infinity]];\n  indices = Association @ Table[gluons[[i]] -> {Symbol[\"mu\" \
<> ToString[i]], Symbol[\"nu\" <> ToString[i]]}, {i, Length[gluons]}];\n  \
conj = ComplexConjugate[amp];\n  expr = amp conj;\n  expr = expr /. (With[{l \
= #, lTag = tag[#]}, Spinor[c_. Momentum[l, D], m_, o_] :> Spinor[c \
Momentum[lTag, D], m, o]] & /@ {pa, p});\n  expr = expr /. \
Flatten[Table[{Momentum[Polarization[l, I, ___], D] -> \
LorentzIndex[indices[l][[1]], D],\n    Momentum[Polarization[l, -I, ___], D] \
-> LorentzIndex[indices[l][[2]], D]}, {l, gluons}]];\n  expr = expr Times @@ \
Table[polarizationSum[l, indices[l][[1]], indices[l][[2]]], {l, gluons}];\n  \
expr = FermionSpinSum[FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit[expr]];\n  expr = expr /. \
{DiracGamma[Momentum[tag[pa], D], D] :> GS[pa].GA[5].GS[sa], \
DiracGamma[Momentum[tag[p], D], D] :> GS[p].GA[5].GS[sc]};\n  expr = \
DiracSimplify[expr, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] // Contract;\n  expr = \
SUNSimplify[expr, Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF -> False] // Contract // \
ExpandScalarProduct;\n  colourFactors[Together[average[ch] expr/gs^4 /. u -> \
-s - t]]/If[spinCase === \"XX\", axes[\"Lengths\"], 1]];", "Input"], 
  Cell["transfer = Association @ Table[name[ch] -> Module[{nn4 = square[ch, \
\"NN\"], xx4 = square[ch, \"XX\"]},\n  <|\"NN\" -> nn4, \"XX\" -> xx4, \
\"Collins\" -> Factor[(nn4 + xx4)/2]|>], {ch, \
channels}];\nTableForm[Normal[Map[Simplify[#[\"Collins\"] /. D -> 4] &, \
transfer]]]", "Input"], Cell["Checks against the paper", "Section"], 
  Cell["In four dimensions the two components agree in every channel; the \
Collins projection is compared with the table of the paper, the control \
channels and their charge conjugates must vanish, and the charge-conjugate \
channels must equal their representatives.", "Text"], 
  Cell["K = (Nc^2 - 1)/Nc^2;\nexpected = <|\"q qp -> q\" -> -K s u/t^2, \"q \
qpb -> q\" -> -K s u/t^2, \"q q -> q\" -> -K s u/t^2 + K s/(Nc t),\n  \"q qb \
-> q\" -> -K s u/t^2 + K u/(Nc t), \"q qb -> qb\" -> -K/Nc, \"q g -> q\" -> \
-2 s u/t^2 + K|>;\ncheck[expr_] := Simplify[expr /. D -> 4 /. u -> -s - \
t];\nRequire[And @@ Table[check[transfer[ch][\"NN\"] - transfer[ch][\"XX\"]] \
=== 0, {ch, Keys[transfer]}], \"The two transverse components differ in four \
dimensions\"];\ndifferences = Association @ KeyValueMap[#1 -> \
check[transfer[#1][\"Collins\"] - #2] &, expected];\nRequire[And @@ (# === 0 \
& /@ Values[differences]), \"A resolved transverse Born term differs from the \
paper\", differences];\nRequire[And @@ \
Table[check[transfer[name[ch]][\"Collins\"]] === 0, {ch, Join[controls, \
conjugate /@ controls]}], \"A control channel does not \
vanish\"];\nRequire[And @@ Table[check[transfer[name[ch]][\"Collins\"] - \
transfer[name[conjugate[ch]]][\"Collins\"]] === 0, {ch, representatives}],\n  \
\"A charge-conjugate channel differs from its \
representative\"];\ndifferences", "Input"], Cell["Save", "Section"], 
  Cell["result = <|\"Transfer\" -> transfer, \"Channels\" -> Map[name, \
channels], \"Variables\" -> \"s, t (u = -s-t), D, Nc; divided by gs^4; first \
incoming parton polarized, tagged parton c\"|>;\nSaveResult[\"ResolvedBorn\", \
result];\nKeys[transfer]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
